# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Study-tutor specific
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Bring-your-own-sources — operator-acquired study guides stay on the
# operator's machine. See domains/gcse-english/sources/README.md and
# domains/gcse-english/sources/CONTRIBUTING-CORPUS.md.
# TASK-RAG-001 (2026-05-08): extend to .txt and .xhtml so Standard Ebooks
# plain-text downloads (the canonical primary-text source per CONTRIBUTING-CORPUS.md)
# also stay out of the repo. The ingestion script (scripts/ingest_corpus.py)
# walks domains/*/sources/ but the texts themselves never get committed.
# 2026-05-10: extend to .md / .markdown so Docling-VLM-rendered primary texts
# (per RUNBOOK-primary-texts-docling-vlm.md) also stay out — most are in-
# copyright (e.g. An Inspector Calls, AQA Power & Conflict anthology) and
# CONTRIBUTING-CORPUS.md §4 already lists .md as never-commit.
domains/*/sources/*.pdf
domains/*/sources/**/*.pdf
domains/*/sources/*.PDF
domains/*/sources/**/*.PDF
domains/*/sources/*.epub
domains/*/sources/**/*.epub
domains/*/sources/*.txt
domains/*/sources/**/*.txt
domains/*/sources/*.xhtml
domains/*/sources/**/*.xhtml
domains/*/sources/*.md
domains/*/sources/**/*.md
domains/*/sources/*.markdown
domains/*/sources/**/*.markdown
# Re-include the policy docs that live at the top of sources/ — these
# describe the corpus contribution rules and ARE committed.
!domains/*/sources/CONTRIBUTING-CORPUS.md
!domains/*/sources/README.md

# In-copyright / unusable source material kept out of `domains/*/sources/`
# so the loader (load_corpus) never walks into it. Files here are operator-
# acquired and stay on the operator's machine — see TASK-RAG-001A discussion
# notes (2026-05-08) for why each file lives here rather than in the
# corpus tree.
docs/research/in-copyright-quarantine/

# RAG knowledge layer persistence (Phase 1 onward).
# DECISION-RAG-001 standardises on ``data/chroma/`` as the per-project
# persist root; the older ``chroma/`` / ``chroma_data*/`` entries stay for
# back-compat with any pre-decision local checkouts that already wrote there.
chroma/
chroma_data/
chroma_data*/
data/chroma/

# Synthetic training data generated by agentic-dataset-factory
output/train.jsonl
output/**/train.jsonl
train.jsonl

# Model artefacts — never checked in, always pulled/built locally
*.gguf
*.safetensors
models/
adapters/
merged-16bit/
merged-fp16/

# Re-include Python boundary-adapter packages and their tests. The bare
# ``adapters/`` rule above is for ML model artefacts (LoRA etc.) but is
# unanchored, so it matches every ``adapters/`` directory in the tree.
# Each Python adapters package needs an explicit re-include pair below
# or its files are silently dropped at git-add time — the failure mode
# behind TASK-INV-AB1 (FEAT-6CC5 ``tutoring/adapters/``) and the FEAT-39E1
# autobuild false-completion of 2026-05-08 (NATS-fleet ``adapters/``).
# Add a new pair here whenever a new adapters/ package lands.
!src/study_tutor/tutoring/adapters/
!src/study_tutor/tutoring/adapters/*.py
!tests/unit/tutoring/adapters/
!tests/unit/tutoring/adapters/*.py
!src/study_tutor/adapters/
!src/study_tutor/adapters/*.py
!tests/unit/adapters/
!tests/unit/adapters/*.py

# Local inference scratch
ollama_models/
.ollama/

# Claude Desktop / MCP working artefacts
stdout.log
stderr.log
*.walkthrough.log

# Per-machine Claude Code overrides
.claude/settings.local.json

# GuardKit local-only archive (per /feature-complete spec)
.guardkit/archive/

# GuardKit Graphiti query log (rotated, local-only diagnostics)
.guardkit/graphiti-query-log.jsonl
.guardkit/graphiti-query-log.jsonl.1

# GuardKit autobuild process-tracking sidecars (local-only PID/start/end markers)
.guardkit/autobuild/*/logs/*.pid
.guardkit/autobuild/*/logs/*.start
.guardkit/autobuild/*/logs/*.end

# GuardKit worktrees — `git worktree list` already tracks these via
# .git/worktrees/ metadata; the directories under .guardkit/worktrees/
# are checked-out branches (not files in the parent worktree's tree)
# plus the `nats-core ->` symlink used by docker-build.sh. None of this
# belongs in the main worktree's git index.
.guardkit/worktrees/

